00:04:33.330 --> 00:04:37.780
No one actually really knows what symbol,
if any, Columbus had on his sails, specially

00:04:37.780 --> 00:04:39.240
during the first voyage.

00:04:39.240 --> 00:04:43.800
However almost all depictions of the voyages
show the ships having a red cross on a white

00:04:43.800 --> 00:04:44.800
background.

00:04:44.800 --> 00:04:49.039
This would be very possible as two of the
three ships were caravels which are of Portuguese

00:04:49.039 --> 00:04:51.690
origin who used the red Knights Templar cross.

00:04:51.690 --> 00:04:52.690
(origins of this cross comes from the crusade
same as the English cross hence the similarity)

00:04:52.690 --> 00:04:57.310
Plus to add to this Genoa where Columbus was
from also had a main symbol of a red cross.

00:04:57.310 --> 00:05:01.720
On top of that the Spanish have been known
to use the red cross on a white background

00:05:01.720 --> 00:05:06.469
as well although for them it was suppose to
symbolize the Cross of Saint James which depending

00:05:06.469 --> 00:05:10.020
on how drawn can look very similarly to the
Templar’s cross.

00:05:10.020 --> 00:05:14.540
All this means that it is very likely that
Columbus had a red cross on a white background

00:05:14.540 --> 00:05:18.009
on his ships but again we just don't know
for sure.

